8
00:00:54,460 --> 00:00:56,160
(Na Tae Hoon, Welcome)

9
00:01:05,970 --> 00:01:08,370
(Cheongma General Affairs Data,
Cheongma Vehicle Management)

10
00:01:14,180 --> 00:01:15,180
(Cheongma PR Department:
Document Index)

11
00:01:15,250 --> 00:01:16,880
(Weekly PR Report)

12
00:01:17,080 --> 00:01:20,990
(PR Manager, Na Tae Hoon)

13
00:01:30,630 --> 00:01:33,030
(PR Manager, Na Tae Hoon)

14
00:01:58,020 --> 00:01:59,020
Ms. Joo.

15
00:02:00,230 --> 00:02:01,990
Ms. Ko, what are you doing here?

16
00:02:02,960 --> 00:02:05,060
And so late at night, too?

17
00:02:06,970 --> 00:02:11,470
I was here for a meeting earlier,
and I left my phone behind.

18
00:02:13,100 --> 00:02:15,210
Is that so?

19
00:02:16,170 --> 00:02:17,180
For a second, I thought...

20
00:02:19,110 --> 00:02:21,810
Well, if you left your phone,
that's understandable.

21
00:02:23,180 --> 00:02:25,320
I can't live a single day
without my phone either.

22
00:02:26,920 --> 00:02:28,420
Still, you should be relieved.

23
00:02:29,350 --> 00:02:30,990
You're lucky I was the one
who found you.

24
00:02:31,560 --> 00:02:33,460
What if it'd been someone else?

25
00:02:35,260 --> 00:02:37,560
What would you have done
if you were accused of stealing?

26
00:02:38,060 --> 00:02:39,060
Right?

27
00:02:40,570 --> 00:02:41,570
Right.

28
00:02:42,400 --> 00:02:44,400
So, how are you finding things
at the company?

29
00:02:44,740 --> 00:02:45,740
Are you managing okay?

30
00:02:46,640 --> 00:02:47,640
Yes, it's great.

31
00:02:49,770 --> 00:02:51,140
You were pretty upset last time,
weren't you?

32
00:02:52,540 --> 00:02:54,550
- Pardon?
- Looking back,

33
00:02:54,550 --> 00:02:55,950
I was narrow-minded.

34
00:02:57,050 --> 00:02:59,080
Once you've paid
your debt to society,

35
00:02:59,080 --> 00:03:01,890
it's only right to accept you back.

36
00:03:03,490 --> 00:03:04,490
I'm sure it was upsetting.

37
00:03:06,260 --> 00:03:07,260
Not at all.

38
00:03:08,560 --> 00:03:10,500
Well, thank you for saying so.

39
00:03:11,460 --> 00:03:12,460
All right, then.

40
00:03:13,030 --> 00:03:14,570
You should get going. It's late.

41
00:03:15,700 --> 00:03:16,700
Right, I will.

42
00:03:30,380 --> 00:03:31,380
What?

43
00:03:32,120 --> 00:03:33,820
Were you really caught
by Director Joo?

44
00:03:34,220 --> 00:03:35,220
So what happened?

45
00:03:37,320 --> 00:03:40,890
Fortunately, she bought my excuse,
so I managed to smooth things over.

46
00:03:42,530 --> 00:03:44,030
Well, that's a huge relief.

47
00:03:45,800 --> 00:03:46,800
By the way,

48
00:03:48,030 --> 00:03:50,170
what's Director Joo like?

49
00:03:53,870 --> 00:03:55,210
Her reputation
at the company is good.

50
00:03:56,710 --> 00:03:58,110
As the Chairman's right-hand woman,

51
00:03:58,510 --> 00:04:01,050
she's highly capable
and easy to get along with.

52
00:04:02,210 --> 00:04:03,210
Is that so?

53
00:04:04,650 --> 00:04:06,780
Anyway, we need to be more careful.

54
00:04:09,090 --> 00:04:10,090
I know.

55
00:04:13,060 --> 00:04:14,190
If you caught her in the act,

56
00:04:14,260 --> 00:04:15,830
you should've just called
the police.

57
00:04:15,890 --> 00:04:17,060
Why didn't you?

58
00:04:18,560 --> 00:04:19,560
It's more amusing this way.

59
00:04:20,230 --> 00:04:22,630
She thinks she's being clever,
but she'll tire herself out.

60
00:04:23,600 --> 00:04:25,470
Manager Na, you have
the countermeasures prepared, right?

61
00:04:26,470 --> 00:04:28,110
Of course. Don't worry about that.

62
00:04:29,310 --> 00:04:30,310
Good.

63
00:04:30,510 --> 00:04:31,580
By the way,

64
00:04:31,840 --> 00:04:34,380
CEO Kang has a friend
named Bae Jong Min.

65
00:04:34,880 --> 00:04:36,550
He's a writer and a pundit.

66
00:04:37,580 --> 00:04:38,620
Bae Jong Min?

67
00:04:39,080 --> 00:04:42,320
Yes. See if you can dig up
some dirt on him.

68
00:04:43,290 --> 00:04:45,860
It's always the intellectual types
who act so dignified...

69
00:04:45,920 --> 00:04:47,130
that have the most to hide.

70
00:04:48,190 --> 00:04:49,190
Understood.

71
00:04:55,670 --> 00:04:57,070
Welcome, Chief Cha.

72
00:04:57,500 --> 00:04:58,700
Thank you for having me over.

73
00:04:59,500 --> 00:05:00,910
- This is for you.
- Goodness.

74
00:05:01,310 --> 00:05:02,610
- Is this for me?
- Yes.

75
00:05:04,010 --> 00:05:06,340
How did you know
I like these flowers?

76
00:05:07,610 --> 00:05:08,610
Did you tell him?

77
00:05:09,080 --> 00:05:10,080
No.

78
00:05:10,420 --> 00:05:12,880
How did you know
Mom likes lisianthuses, Seok Jin?

79
00:05:13,890 --> 00:05:16,290
I remember seeing it
in an online article once.

80
00:05:16,720 --> 00:05:18,990
My goodness, you're so thoughtful.

81
00:05:19,620 --> 00:05:20,830
Thank you, Seok Jin.

82
00:05:21,230 --> 00:05:22,690
I'm glad you like them.

83
00:05:23,260 --> 00:05:24,260
They smell wonderful, too.

84
00:05:25,230 --> 00:05:26,700
Gosh, where's my head at?

85
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:29,530
Honey, Seok Jin's here.
Come say hello.

86
00:05:29,930 --> 00:05:31,100
Right, welcome.

87
00:05:32,040 --> 00:05:34,070
Since you're here,
how about a drink?

88
00:05:34,940 --> 00:05:35,940
Sure.

89
00:05:36,170 --> 00:05:37,610
Honey, could you get us
some drinks and snacks?

90
00:05:38,080 --> 00:05:39,580
- Okay.
- Let's go.

91
00:05:40,580 --> 00:05:41,580
Wait.

92
00:05:42,780 --> 00:05:44,320
You stay back.

93
00:05:44,320 --> 00:05:45,820
Why, Mom?

94
00:05:46,350 --> 00:05:48,120
Give them some space today.

95
00:05:50,820 --> 00:05:52,960
Come on. Are you kidding me?

96
00:06:00,100 --> 00:06:02,630
- Allow me.
- It's fine Let's keep it casual.

97
00:06:07,040 --> 00:06:08,140
Here, have a drink.

98
00:06:08,210 --> 00:06:09,210
Thank you.

99
00:06:16,550 --> 00:06:18,120
So why are you here today?

100
00:06:19,080 --> 00:06:20,120
Pardon?

101
00:06:20,850 --> 00:06:22,990
I doubt you came here
just to chat with me.

102
00:06:23,150 --> 00:06:24,920
So, what brings you here?

103
00:06:26,960 --> 00:06:29,990
I wanted to know why you won't
give us your blessing.

104
00:06:31,460 --> 00:06:33,800
You're telling me
you don't know why?

105
00:06:34,170 --> 00:06:35,670
Is it because of my family?

106
00:06:36,370 --> 00:06:37,940
Because we're no help
to Cheongma Group?

107
00:06:38,600 --> 00:06:39,840
So you do know.

108
00:06:40,970 --> 00:06:45,010
My one and only goal
is to make Cheongma...

109
00:06:45,410 --> 00:06:47,910
the top company in the industry.

110
00:06:48,350 --> 00:06:50,550
And to do that,
I desperately need connections.

111
00:06:51,250 --> 00:06:52,550
You know that as well as I do.

112
00:06:53,050 --> 00:06:56,320
There's no stronger alliance
than one made through marriage.

113
00:06:57,960 --> 00:06:58,960
Then,

114
00:07:01,160 --> 00:07:04,130
if I make Cheongma the top company
in the industry,

115
00:07:04,560 --> 00:07:06,500
will you give us your blessing?

116
00:07:06,900 --> 00:07:08,000
What did you say?

117
00:07:08,870 --> 00:07:09,970
Within five years,

118
00:07:10,540 --> 00:07:12,870
I'll make Cheongma the top company
in the industry.

119
00:07:14,110 --> 00:07:16,810
To do that, we need to transition
into a total fashion company,

120
00:07:17,310 --> 00:07:20,040
which is why I plan to launch
a new shoe brand.

121
00:07:20,040 --> 00:07:21,710
If I succeed at all of that,

122
00:07:22,780 --> 00:07:23,780
then will you...

123
00:07:24,920 --> 00:07:26,250
reconsider?

124
00:07:28,950 --> 00:07:30,020
All right.

125
00:07:30,690 --> 00:07:32,520
Now it's my turn to ask a question.

126
00:07:33,790 --> 00:07:36,060
Why make such
an impossible promise...

127
00:07:36,660 --> 00:07:39,860
to marry Hae Ra
when you don't even love her?

128
00:07:41,400 --> 00:07:44,100
I'm a man
who takes promises very seriously.

129
00:07:45,270 --> 00:07:47,840
That's why I intend to keep
my promise to Hae Ra.

130
00:07:48,610 --> 00:07:49,940
Is that the only reason?

131
00:07:52,240 --> 00:07:54,050
Of course, succeeding you as CEO...

132
00:07:54,780 --> 00:07:57,250
and growing Cheongma
into a global company...

133
00:07:57,680 --> 00:08:00,620
is a challenge
I believe is well worth taking on.

134
00:08:02,120 --> 00:08:04,090
You're a smooth talker,
I'll give you that.

135
00:08:06,120 --> 00:08:07,160
But...

136
00:08:07,490 --> 00:08:09,890
I can't stand people
who are all talk.

137
00:08:11,300 --> 00:08:12,360
In any case,

138
00:08:12,830 --> 00:08:16,400
successfully launch
the shoe brand first.

139
00:08:17,470 --> 00:08:18,800
Yes, sir.

140
00:08:19,900 --> 00:08:20,910
Here.

141
00:08:39,260 --> 00:08:40,420
You must be busy
between your daily work...

142
00:08:41,030 --> 00:08:42,930
and investigating
the department managers.

143
00:08:44,300 --> 00:08:45,300
Isn't it exhausting?

144
00:08:46,360 --> 00:08:50,940
This is nothing
compared to life in prison.

145
00:08:52,500 --> 00:08:55,010
Oh, right. Of course.

146
00:08:56,770 --> 00:08:58,740
Anyway, at this rate,

147
00:08:58,810 --> 00:09:00,410
we should be able to find
the real killer by next week.

148
00:09:00,710 --> 00:09:01,710
Well,

149
00:09:01,950 --> 00:09:03,410
if everything goes
according to plan.

150
00:09:04,550 --> 00:09:06,220
I'm suddenly getting nervous.

151
00:09:07,490 --> 00:09:08,490
Why don't we go somewhere...

152
00:09:08,620 --> 00:09:10,690
and grab a cold beer
before calling it a night?

153
00:09:13,190 --> 00:09:14,290
Beer?

154
00:09:15,830 --> 00:09:17,630
Why? You don't want to?

155
00:09:18,260 --> 00:09:19,260
Well, it's...

156
00:09:19,700 --> 00:09:22,300
I'm just a little tired.

157
00:09:24,740 --> 00:09:25,740
Sorry about that.

158
00:09:25,970 --> 00:09:27,770
I was only thinking of myself again.

159
00:09:27,970 --> 00:09:29,170
Hey, we're almost home.

160
00:09:29,470 --> 00:09:30,510
You should head in.

161
00:09:39,250 --> 00:09:40,280
We're here.

162
00:09:42,350 --> 00:09:44,920
I'll definitely
buy you that beer next time.

163
00:09:45,260 --> 00:09:48,390
Okay. Don't worry about it.
Go on and get some rest.

164
00:09:49,260 --> 00:09:51,930
Right. You get some rest too.

165
00:09:51,930 --> 00:09:52,930
Sure.

166
00:10:00,140 --> 00:10:01,370
You're such a fool.

167
00:10:10,610 --> 00:10:11,720
Why are you just standing there?

168
00:10:11,880 --> 00:10:13,520
Do my words mean nothing to you?

169
00:10:14,050 --> 00:10:16,790
Didn't I tell you
to stop hanging out with Eun Seol?

170
00:10:17,490 --> 00:10:18,490
You did.

171
00:10:18,560 --> 00:10:19,590
And?

172
00:10:19,590 --> 00:10:22,360
And I told you
that I don't care about rumors.

173
00:10:22,390 --> 00:10:23,430
Hey, Seo Hyun Jae.

174
00:10:23,630 --> 00:10:25,600
I'm not in the mood,
so just leave me alone.

175
00:10:28,700 --> 00:10:30,270
I can't believe him.

176
00:10:31,170 --> 00:10:32,170
Mom.

177
00:10:33,300 --> 00:10:36,970
Why can't Uncle and Eun Seol
hang out together?

178
00:10:38,340 --> 00:10:39,710
You don't need to know.

179
00:10:40,580 --> 00:10:44,580
Why? Are you worried Uncle
and Eun Seol might start dating?

180
00:10:46,380 --> 00:10:48,020
You shouldn't say things like that.

181
00:10:50,720 --> 00:10:51,790
Wait a minute.

182
00:10:52,390 --> 00:10:55,430
Do you even know
what that word means?

183
00:10:55,760 --> 00:10:56,760
What? Dating?

184
00:10:57,500 --> 00:10:59,200
Of course I do.

185
00:10:59,400 --> 00:11:01,800
That's when you become
boyfriend and girlfriend.

186
00:11:02,730 --> 00:11:03,730
Right?

187
00:11:05,100 --> 00:11:07,710
Anyway, you shouldn't say
things like that.

188
00:11:07,910 --> 00:11:08,910
Got it?

189
00:11:09,440 --> 00:11:11,140
Is dating a bad thing?

190
00:11:11,440 --> 00:11:12,840
Seo Teun Teun.

191
00:11:13,340 --> 00:11:14,510
Fine.

192
00:11:19,850 --> 00:11:22,750
- Are you a little drunk?
- I'm fine.

193
00:11:23,050 --> 00:11:24,160
I'll be going now.

194
00:11:24,220 --> 00:11:27,690
Okay. Did you have a good talk
with the CEO?

195
00:11:28,360 --> 00:11:29,530
Yes, I guess.

196
00:11:30,090 --> 00:11:31,230
Really?

197
00:11:32,160 --> 00:11:33,960
Then, I'll see you at work tomorrow.

198
00:11:34,430 --> 00:11:37,070
- Sure.
- Dad, Seok Jin's leaving.

199
00:11:37,130 --> 00:11:39,840
Let him be.
He must be tired from drinking.

200
00:11:40,300 --> 00:11:41,910
Let's go then. I'll drive you.

201
00:11:41,970 --> 00:11:43,240
I can just call a driver.

202
00:11:43,310 --> 00:11:47,010
I'm saying I'll be your driver.
I won't take long, Mom.

203
00:11:47,040 --> 00:11:48,110
Sure.

204
00:11:48,380 --> 00:11:49,750
Well, I'll be going now.

205
00:11:50,250 --> 00:11:52,080
It's pretty dark out, so drive safe.

206
00:11:52,080 --> 00:11:53,280
I will.

207
00:11:56,620 --> 00:11:58,420
Goodness, you're in bed already?

208
00:12:00,320 --> 00:12:02,330
Honey, Seok Jin just left.

209
00:12:05,100 --> 00:12:06,130
Are you asleep?

210
00:12:07,900 --> 00:12:08,900
Yes.

211
00:12:10,330 --> 00:12:12,000
You say you're asleep,
but you just answered.

212
00:12:14,840 --> 00:12:15,910
So?

213
00:12:16,170 --> 00:12:18,640
What did you and Seok Jin
talk about?

214
00:12:21,350 --> 00:12:22,610
Honey.

215
00:12:23,850 --> 00:12:26,520
Whatever. I'm tired.

216
00:12:37,960 --> 00:12:39,160
Hey, you're home.

217
00:12:39,530 --> 00:12:40,800
You're still awake, Mom?

218
00:12:41,100 --> 00:12:42,100
Yes.

219
00:12:45,300 --> 00:12:46,900
I'm here too, Ms. Park.

220
00:12:48,110 --> 00:12:50,310
Right. Hey.

221
00:12:51,510 --> 00:12:53,880
Gosh, I'm tired.

222
00:12:54,010 --> 00:12:56,750
Mr. Seok Jin,
I'm going to bed first.

223
00:12:58,420 --> 00:13:00,850
Okay, sure. Good night, Mom.

224
00:13:01,490 --> 00:13:03,090
Good night, Ms. Park.

225
00:13:09,290 --> 00:13:11,660
So? What did you talk about
with my dad?

226
00:13:12,800 --> 00:13:15,970
What else would I talk about
with the CEO besides work?

227
00:13:16,570 --> 00:13:18,740
Didn't you tell him
you wanted to marry me?

228
00:13:22,240 --> 00:13:23,410
Didn't you?

229
00:13:23,940 --> 00:13:25,080
I did.

230
00:13:25,540 --> 00:13:26,540
You did?

231
00:13:27,410 --> 00:13:28,480
And what did he say?

232
00:13:30,610 --> 00:13:33,080
You know the CEO is
against our marriage.

233
00:13:34,820 --> 00:13:36,850
So just because he's against it,

234
00:13:36,920 --> 00:13:39,290
you caved and told him
you wouldn't marry me?

235
00:13:41,230 --> 00:13:42,230
Really?

236
00:13:48,670 --> 00:13:49,670
Kang Hae Ra.

237
00:13:50,630 --> 00:13:51,940
I'm going to try.

238
00:13:55,610 --> 00:13:58,710
I'm going to work to get
the CEO's blessing for our marriage.

239
00:13:59,740 --> 00:14:00,740
Really?

240
00:14:02,250 --> 00:14:04,220
So, can you trust me and wait?

241
00:14:04,980 --> 00:14:06,650
Of course.

242
00:14:09,520 --> 00:14:11,460
You'd better not disappoint me.

243
00:14:11,660 --> 00:14:13,520
And I won't disappoint you.

244
00:14:13,860 --> 00:14:17,660
I get it.
How could I ever disappoint you?

245
00:14:28,570 --> 00:14:29,610
I trust you.

246
00:14:30,240 --> 00:14:31,240
But,

247
00:14:33,110 --> 00:14:34,710
this time, when you're ready,

248
00:14:35,350 --> 00:14:37,350
please tell me in good time.

249
00:14:47,320 --> 00:14:49,660
(Cheongma)

250
00:14:54,430 --> 00:14:56,870
Good morning.
Did everyone have a good weekend?

251
00:14:57,670 --> 00:15:00,000
Yes. Did you have
a good weekend, Ms. Kang?

252
00:15:00,270 --> 00:15:03,310
Did something good happen?
You seem to be in a good mood.

253
00:15:04,410 --> 00:15:05,410
Do I?

254
00:15:06,640 --> 00:15:09,780
Did you have a nice time
with Chief Cha?

255
00:15:12,280 --> 00:15:13,780
That's enough
with the morning greetings.

256
00:15:13,850 --> 00:15:14,920
Shall we start the meeting?

257
00:15:19,060 --> 00:15:21,960
- Did you look into Bae Jong Min?
- Yes.

258
00:15:22,730 --> 00:15:26,030
But there's nothing dirty about him
that's newsworthy.

259
00:15:27,100 --> 00:15:30,100
What? No plagiarism allegations
or tax evasion charges?

260
00:15:30,530 --> 00:15:31,540
No, ma'am.

261
00:15:31,770 --> 00:15:33,940
What about his personal life?
Any trouble with women?

262
00:15:34,670 --> 00:15:36,740
He's clean on that front too.

263
00:15:36,810 --> 00:15:39,510
The only women he meets
are reporters.

264
00:15:40,640 --> 00:15:41,650
Reporters?

265
00:15:42,280 --> 00:15:44,110
Yes. There's one
female political reporter...

266
00:15:44,110 --> 00:15:45,750
he hangs out with often.

267
00:15:45,850 --> 00:15:48,750
They meet up for drinks sometimes,
but that's all.

268
00:15:49,650 --> 00:15:51,490
Then link him with the reporter.

269
00:15:52,790 --> 00:15:53,790
Pardon?

270
00:15:55,190 --> 00:15:56,560
Is this your first day
working with me?

271
00:15:56,890 --> 00:15:58,630
Are you dense or what?

272
00:15:59,100 --> 00:16:01,270
Do I have to spell out
how to link him with the reporter?

273
00:16:02,500 --> 00:16:04,200
I'm sorry. I'll take care of it.

274
00:16:06,640 --> 00:16:07,710
Also, this...

275
00:16:08,110 --> 00:16:09,110
What is it?

276
00:16:09,840 --> 00:16:12,010
Professor Hong sent it to you.

277
00:16:12,610 --> 00:16:13,810
I think it's a book.

278
00:16:14,350 --> 00:16:16,250
- You can go.
- Yes, ma'am.

279
00:16:20,220 --> 00:16:22,650
Who reads this stuff? Unbelievable.

280
00:16:26,190 --> 00:16:27,190
What's this?

281
00:16:30,930 --> 00:16:34,130
He must be desperate, seeing
as he's throwing money around.

282
00:16:42,810 --> 00:16:43,810
Excuse me.

283
00:16:45,210 --> 00:16:46,210
Me?

284
00:16:46,710 --> 00:16:49,750
Who else would I be talking to?

285
00:16:52,280 --> 00:16:53,280
Excuse me.

286
00:16:53,880 --> 00:16:54,890
What?

287
00:16:55,550 --> 00:16:56,850
Why are you so prickly?

288
00:16:58,390 --> 00:17:00,620
Me? You think I'm prickly?

289
00:17:00,860 --> 00:17:02,660
You don't know you're prickly?

290
00:17:04,290 --> 00:17:07,360
In my entire life,
no one has ever said that to me.

291
00:17:08,300 --> 00:17:09,930
Then you must not have any friends.

292
00:17:10,600 --> 00:17:11,600
What did you say?

293
00:17:12,370 --> 00:17:14,740
Well, that would explain
why you've never heard it.

294
00:17:16,510 --> 00:17:19,110
For your information,
I have a lot of friends.

295
00:17:20,540 --> 00:17:21,810
Whatever.

296
00:17:22,250 --> 00:17:24,450
- What did you want?
- So, I...

297
00:17:25,380 --> 00:17:28,650
Wait, what was I going to say?

298
00:17:29,520 --> 00:17:32,490
You made me forget
by saying all that nonsense.

299
00:17:33,190 --> 00:17:35,190
Now it's my fault you forgot
what you were going to say?

300
00:17:35,260 --> 00:17:38,060
Anyway, I'm not prickly.

301
00:17:38,460 --> 00:17:41,100
So stop making
a completely normal person sound strange.

302
00:17:42,830 --> 00:17:43,930
Got it?

303
00:17:52,110 --> 00:17:54,210
Who were you talking to for so long?

304
00:17:55,580 --> 00:17:56,580
Mi Rae.

305
00:17:56,910 --> 00:17:58,380
Who's Mi Rae?

306
00:17:59,550 --> 00:18:00,580
Teun Teun's mom.

307
00:18:00,880 --> 00:18:04,420
Then just say she's Teun Teun's mom.
What's with calling her Mi Rae?

308
00:18:04,420 --> 00:18:05,460
Don't call her that.

309
00:18:05,820 --> 00:18:07,060
Grandma, come on.

310
00:18:07,390 --> 00:18:09,930
I'm just calling Mi Rae by her name.
What's wrong with that?

311
00:18:10,290 --> 00:18:12,360
If I tell you not to, then don't.

312
00:18:12,900 --> 00:18:15,900
I'm saying this for your own good.

313
00:18:17,330 --> 00:18:20,940
Anyway, what were you two
talking about for so long?

314
00:18:21,810 --> 00:18:24,710
How would I know?
She called me out of the blue,

315
00:18:24,880 --> 00:18:26,110
only to forget
what she wanted to say.

316
00:18:26,210 --> 00:18:27,210
What?

317
00:18:27,780 --> 00:18:30,550
That shameless woman is making
a move on him, isn't she?

318
00:18:31,920 --> 00:18:34,120
I need to give her a warning.
This won't do.

319
00:18:35,450 --> 00:18:39,720
Mom, don't you even think
about saying anything harsh to her.

320
00:18:39,790 --> 00:18:42,490
Don't forget
that we're living here for free.

321
00:18:42,560 --> 00:18:46,230
As if. We pay our rent on time.

322
00:18:46,900 --> 00:18:48,530
That's some interesting logic.

323
00:18:48,770 --> 00:18:51,370
Anyone would think
you're the one paying the rent.

324
00:18:57,910 --> 00:18:59,110
I remember now.

325
00:19:00,610 --> 00:19:02,680
I was going to tell him
to keep his sister in line.

326
00:19:03,080 --> 00:19:05,020
How could you forget that, Mi Rae?

327
00:19:11,720 --> 00:19:12,920
Honey!

328
00:19:14,220 --> 00:19:15,390
Did you see the article?

329
00:19:15,930 --> 00:19:16,930
What article?

330
00:19:17,590 --> 00:19:20,530
Haven't you heard about
Bae Jong Min's alleged affair?

331
00:19:20,860 --> 00:19:23,400
What?
Oh, come on. That's ridiculous.

332
00:19:23,470 --> 00:19:25,640
He's not that kind of person.

333
00:19:25,700 --> 00:19:27,440
It must be someone
with the same name.

334
00:19:27,770 --> 00:19:29,110
Look at this.

335
00:19:29,240 --> 00:19:30,510
Still don't believe me?

336
00:19:31,480 --> 00:19:33,280
(Writer and Pundit Bae Jong Min's
Alleged Affair with a Reporter)

337
00:19:34,750 --> 00:19:36,580
Wait, hold on a second.

338
00:19:36,810 --> 00:19:38,620
It's him, right? Unbelievable.

339
00:19:40,450 --> 00:19:43,220
The phone is turned off.
You'll be connected to voicemail.

340
00:19:43,220 --> 00:19:44,250
After the beep...

341
00:19:44,250 --> 00:19:47,060
- He's not picking up?
- His phone is off.

342
00:19:47,320 --> 00:19:51,190
Anyway, I've no intention of putting
Jong Min on our company's board,

343
00:19:51,190 --> 00:19:52,200
so keep that in mind.

344
00:19:52,630 --> 00:19:54,300
Now that this has happened,

345
00:19:54,360 --> 00:19:56,600
I'm not going to insist
on him either.

346
00:19:57,130 --> 00:19:59,370
- I'll look for someone else...
- No.

347
00:20:00,300 --> 00:20:03,210
I'll take care of appointing
the new director myself.

348
00:20:03,940 --> 00:20:04,940
Honey.

349
00:20:05,780 --> 00:20:07,740
I'm the Chairman
of the Scholarship Foundation.

350
00:20:08,410 --> 00:20:12,380
If you don't trust me that much,
you can vet them yourself later.

351
00:20:21,060 --> 00:20:23,460
Who would be a good fit?

352
00:20:24,060 --> 00:20:26,900
You still don't have anyone in mind?

353
00:20:27,260 --> 00:20:29,270
I just assumed it'd be Bae Jong Min,

354
00:20:29,330 --> 00:20:31,100
so I wasn't even thinking about it.

355
00:20:31,370 --> 00:20:35,140
But who could've guessed
something this awful would happen?

356
00:20:35,240 --> 00:20:38,610
Still, it's a relief we found out
before the director was appointed.

357
00:20:40,010 --> 00:20:44,780
That's true.
So, is there anyone you'd recommend?

358
00:20:45,920 --> 00:20:47,020
Well...

359
00:20:47,080 --> 00:20:49,420
No one in my circle comes to mind.

360
00:20:50,020 --> 00:20:51,890
How about someone from your clubs,

361
00:20:52,120 --> 00:20:54,160
or anyone you know
who might be suitable?

362
00:20:55,260 --> 00:20:56,430
My clubs?

363
00:20:57,560 --> 00:20:58,860
Like your flower arrangement club.

364
00:20:58,930 --> 00:21:00,560
You're in a calligraphy club too.

365
00:21:01,430 --> 00:21:03,400
Since Director Han was a professor,

366
00:21:03,630 --> 00:21:05,700
another former professor
would be a solid replacement.

367
00:21:07,500 --> 00:21:09,870
Wait, there is one person.

368
00:21:10,670 --> 00:21:11,680
Who?

369
00:21:12,540 --> 00:21:15,810
Professor Hong Seok Gyu.
He retired last year.

370
00:21:15,980 --> 00:21:18,620
He's in my calligraphy club.

371
00:21:19,250 --> 00:21:21,920
I see. Then he sounds perfect.

372
00:21:22,750 --> 00:21:25,490
Why didn't I think of him?

373
00:21:25,960 --> 00:21:27,760
Thank you, Director Joo.

374
00:21:27,820 --> 00:21:30,090
I knew I could count on you.

375
00:21:31,530 --> 00:21:33,130
What a relief.

376
00:21:34,030 --> 00:21:35,770
Then the only one left is...

377
00:21:37,130 --> 00:21:38,300
The PR Manager.

378
00:21:39,370 --> 00:21:42,040
The one we couldn't confirm
because of Director Joo?

379
00:21:42,510 --> 00:21:43,510
Yes.

380
00:21:44,510 --> 00:21:47,910
Do you think Manager Na Tae Hoon
is connected to the real killer?

381
00:21:48,050 --> 00:21:52,250
Everyone else has an alibi,
so theoretically, yes.

382
00:21:53,320 --> 00:21:55,450
He didn't seem like
that kind of person.

383
00:21:55,750 --> 00:21:56,890
Actually,

384
00:21:57,190 --> 00:21:59,820
I happened to run into him
the other day.

385
00:22:00,490 --> 00:22:02,460
He seems like a really great guy
on the surface.

386
00:22:02,630 --> 00:22:04,030
He's always so cheerful
when he says hello.

387
00:22:04,490 --> 00:22:07,230
Yes, he was the same way with me.

388
00:22:08,170 --> 00:22:09,270
But there's something...

389
00:22:10,500 --> 00:22:13,140
Something feels off about him.

390
00:22:14,140 --> 00:22:19,080
I saw it often in prison.
People who seem fake.

391
00:22:24,180 --> 00:22:25,620
How's it going?

392
00:22:25,780 --> 00:22:27,220
Have you found the real killer?

393
00:22:27,520 --> 00:22:28,520
Not yet.

394
00:22:28,790 --> 00:22:30,120
What's taking so long?

395
00:22:30,520 --> 00:22:31,760
It'll be over soon.

396
00:22:32,220 --> 00:22:34,020
Is there anything else
I can do to help?

397
00:22:34,390 --> 00:22:35,460
No.

398
00:22:35,830 --> 00:22:37,290
I just need to check on
one person tomorrow.

399
00:22:38,160 --> 00:22:40,900
So tomorrow, we'll find out
who the real killer is?

400
00:22:42,030 --> 00:22:44,530
Well, as long as
there are no surprises.

401
00:22:45,170 --> 00:22:47,500
Gosh, my heart is racing.

402
00:22:47,570 --> 00:22:49,570
Okay, then be careful
until the very end.

403
00:22:50,070 --> 00:22:51,140
All right.

404
00:22:54,640 --> 00:22:55,950
You scared me!

405
00:22:56,280 --> 00:22:59,750
Do you want to give your son
a heart attack?

406
00:22:59,920 --> 00:23:02,550
What's wrong with you?
What did I do?

407
00:23:05,220 --> 00:23:07,290
Tell me. What's going on?

408
00:23:08,490 --> 00:23:09,490
What do you mean?

409
00:23:10,190 --> 00:23:11,530
Are you really not going to tell me?

410
00:23:12,360 --> 00:23:13,830
Come on.

411
00:23:15,130 --> 00:23:18,400
It's almost over,
so please wait a little longer.

412
00:23:18,470 --> 00:23:19,670
I'll spill everything
when it's over,

413
00:23:19,670 --> 00:23:22,840
whether you want
to hear it or not. Okay?

414
00:23:22,910 --> 00:23:24,070
What the...

415
00:23:28,650 --> 00:23:30,950
What on earth are they up to?

416
00:23:35,550 --> 00:23:37,690
Everyone, let's go to lunch.

417
00:23:37,890 --> 00:23:38,920
- Sure.
- Okay.

418
00:23:40,760 --> 00:23:41,760
What should we get?

419
00:23:42,830 --> 00:23:43,890
How about...

420
00:23:43,890 --> 00:23:45,400
- Kongguksu?
- Kongguksu? Not really.

421
00:23:59,910 --> 00:24:04,550
(PR Manager, Na Tae Hoon)

422
00:24:12,460 --> 00:24:13,520
(Na Tae Hoon, Welcome)

423
00:24:20,330 --> 00:24:22,730
(June 5: No scheduled appointments)

424
00:24:40,450 --> 00:24:41,450
(Meeting with Hanbit's Kim Seong Sik,
2 p.m.)

425
00:24:43,120 --> 00:24:44,390
What the heck?

426
00:24:45,220 --> 00:24:47,090
Manager Na had a meeting
that day too?

427
00:24:59,870 --> 00:25:01,570
Manager Na has an alibi too?

428
00:25:02,640 --> 00:25:06,680
Yes. Apparently, he had a meeting
with a client that day.

429
00:25:08,010 --> 00:25:09,310
How can that be?

430
00:25:10,280 --> 00:25:11,620
If it isn't Manager Na either,

431
00:25:11,880 --> 00:25:13,620
then we're out of suspects.

432
00:25:14,820 --> 00:25:15,890
Exactly.

433
00:25:19,560 --> 00:25:21,190
Where did we go wrong?

434
00:25:22,260 --> 00:25:23,790
I really don't know.

435
00:25:25,460 --> 00:25:27,230
Has everything we've done so far...

436
00:25:27,330 --> 00:25:28,730
been for nothing?

437
00:25:30,830 --> 00:25:33,300
Still, we have to check it out.

438
00:25:38,880 --> 00:25:41,410
Director Joo, please say hello.

439
00:25:41,650 --> 00:25:45,580
This is Professor Hong Seok Gyu,
who'll be our newest board member.

440
00:25:46,720 --> 00:25:47,720
Is that right?

441
00:25:47,850 --> 00:25:50,490
It's a pleasure to meet you.
I'm Joo Mi Ran.

442
00:25:51,350 --> 00:25:52,760
Oh, right.

443
00:25:53,360 --> 00:25:54,590
Hello.

444
00:25:55,830 --> 00:25:58,800
Professor Hong, isn't this
your first time meeting her?

445
00:25:59,360 --> 00:26:00,600
Yes, that's right.

446
00:26:02,130 --> 00:26:05,640
Director Joo is someone
I couldn't do without.

447
00:26:06,300 --> 00:26:07,570
Is that so?

448
00:26:08,200 --> 00:26:10,510
You're too kind, ma'am.

449
00:26:11,640 --> 00:26:14,480
She's the driving force
behind the foundation's affairs,

450
00:26:14,710 --> 00:26:17,910
so if you have any questions,
you can just ask her.

451
00:26:18,380 --> 00:26:19,450
Yes, I understand.

452
00:26:23,990 --> 00:26:24,990
Excuse me for a moment.

453
00:26:25,060 --> 00:26:26,120
Please, feel free to talk...

454
00:26:26,120 --> 00:26:27,560
- among yourselves.
- Sure.

455
00:26:27,560 --> 00:26:28,760
Yes, Professor.

456
00:26:29,490 --> 00:26:30,490
Yes, of course.

457
00:26:39,740 --> 00:26:41,370
Congratulations, Professor Hong.

458
00:26:42,210 --> 00:26:43,210
Thank you.

459
00:26:43,610 --> 00:26:46,440
I'll forever be
in your debt, Ms. Joo.

460
00:26:50,280 --> 00:26:52,480
What is this?

461
00:26:54,680 --> 00:26:56,390
Are you kidding me with that?

462
00:26:57,550 --> 00:27:00,320
It's not what you think. This is...

463
00:27:00,620 --> 00:27:01,990
I don't need anything else.

464
00:27:02,890 --> 00:27:04,190
You just need to be on my side.

465
00:27:04,930 --> 00:27:05,960
Do you understand?

466
00:27:06,560 --> 00:27:11,130
Oh, of course. Without a doubt.
Don't you worry about that.

467
00:27:17,810 --> 00:27:18,810
Come in.

468
00:27:25,220 --> 00:27:27,950
Hello, I'm Ko Eun Seol.
I called earlier.

469
00:27:28,280 --> 00:27:29,820
You're Team Leader Kim Seong Sik,
correct?

470
00:27:30,150 --> 00:27:31,820
Yes, that's me.

471
00:27:32,560 --> 00:27:33,560
Please, have a seat.

472
00:27:39,500 --> 00:27:42,270
You wanted to inquire
about a new product launch event?

473
00:27:42,600 --> 00:27:44,770
Yes, I was hoping to get a quote.

474
00:27:45,540 --> 00:27:47,340
What size event are you thinking of?

475
00:27:48,140 --> 00:27:50,270
The details are
in the materials I sent.

476
00:27:50,340 --> 00:27:51,470
You'll know when you see them.

477
00:27:51,940 --> 00:27:53,010
I see.

478
00:27:55,750 --> 00:27:58,920
I'm sorry,
but my throat is a bit dry.

479
00:27:58,980 --> 00:28:00,850
Could I have something to drink?

480
00:28:01,450 --> 00:28:02,490
Oh, where are my manners?

481
00:28:02,550 --> 00:28:03,850
Please wait a moment.

482
00:28:19,740 --> 00:28:23,910
(2 p.m., Meeting with
Manager Na Tae Hoon from Cheongma)

483
00:28:38,020 --> 00:28:39,520
The other entries are written
in the exact same ink.

484
00:28:39,590 --> 00:28:41,930
(2 p.m., Meeting with
Manager Na Tae Hoon from Cheongma)

485
00:28:42,030 --> 00:28:44,290
So why does this day's entry...

486
00:28:51,170 --> 00:28:52,700
The handwriting...

487
00:28:53,740 --> 00:28:54,800
(2 p.m., Meeting with
Manager Na Tae Hoon from Cheongma)

488
00:28:55,110 --> 00:28:56,170
Then...

489
00:29:10,790 --> 00:29:13,290
(Meeting with Hanbit's Kim Seong Sik,
2 p.m.)

490
00:29:14,890 --> 00:29:15,930
What the heck?

491
00:29:17,090 --> 00:29:18,700
Manager Na had a meeting
that day too?

492
00:29:20,560 --> 00:29:21,760
Was this added for me to see?

493
00:29:58,770 --> 00:30:02,470
(A Trap Called Desire)

494
00:30:02,710 --> 00:30:04,640
I'm trusting you on this.
I love you.

495
00:30:04,840 --> 00:30:06,510
I knew they were spending
a lot of time together.

496
00:30:06,580 --> 00:30:07,740
I didn't realize they were an item.

497
00:30:07,910 --> 00:30:09,210
What's your relationship
with Eun Seol?

498
00:30:09,410 --> 00:30:11,180
Does what we have
seem that special to you?

499
00:30:12,450 --> 00:30:14,980
Pig's feet? Come on. Have you
ever seen trotters this sexy?

500
00:30:15,190 --> 00:30:16,190
Pig's feet?

501
00:30:16,250 --> 00:30:18,350
I'm literally the Chairman
of the scholarship foundation,

502
00:30:18,560 --> 00:30:20,320
so why can't I appoint
a single director the way I want?

503
00:30:20,520 --> 00:30:21,790
Director Joo,
you need to take one for the team.

504
00:30:21,930 --> 00:30:23,760
Was it your recommendation,
Director Joo?

505
00:30:23,860 --> 00:30:26,730
Are you that dense?
What exactly have you been doing?

506
00:30:26,930 --> 00:30:28,060
So what do we do now?

507
00:30:28,430 --> 00:30:29,670
For the first time in ten years,

508
00:30:29,670 --> 00:30:31,770
they're going to be scared
because of me.

509
00:30:31,970 --> 00:30:34,240
Can't I enjoy that just a bit?

510
00:30:34,900 --> 00:30:36,910
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
